 #:seon.task{:id "17027736987a"
             :name "boot-publication-phases-are-invisible"
             :kind :function
             :intent "A boot resume publication runs before arm-host-program!, so no profile cell observes it and refresh-source!'s explain-slow says nothing; *source-progress!* is bound nowhere (report-source-progress! is a no-op outside tests), so its phase lines vanish. The 132 s store->branch layer of the e405f51be boot could only be split by replaying the publication on a scratch branch (tmp/perf-boot-opus/replay.clj). Carry the boot publication's phase milliseconds in its result and the instance's readiness."
             :must-read #{seon.cluster/refresh-source! seon.cluster/populate-source!}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/perf-boot-opus-2026-09-26.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "the-save-gate-cannot-prove-a-commit"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Every JVM runs a committed archive (data/source/<sha>), so `bin/test-check default --gate --changed-path <checkout file>` refuses at seon.cluster/publication-paths (cluster.clj:2954, 'Changed paths lie outside the JVM's source directory') and a lane cannot prove a change on default before landing. Measured 2026-09-27 by shrink-web-opus (tmp/shrink-web-opus/gate-s1p2.out). The gate should take a commit (a lane's commit or HEAD) and publish from its archive, running the reaching tests on a candidate branch and adopting only on green, so prove-before-land works under the archive law without restarting default."
             :must-read #{seon.cluster/publication-paths seon.cluster/refresh-source!}
             :evidence #{"tmp/shrink-web-opus/gate-s1p2.out"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-test-adoption-moves-the-jvms-loaded-identity"
             :kind :function
             :intent "seon.sci.eval/loaded-identity is one process-wide atom, and call-with-program-change (from development-source-refresh!) advances it to the commit the adopting store published. A test that boots a cluster on its own root and store and adopts there (seon.adoption-contract-freshness-test calls refresh-source! with a development cluster) therefore renames the JVM's loaded program after a commit of another store, and later test requests' seon.test/arm-first-loads! open that commit through seon.cluster.source/database. That is JVM-global test state (CLAUDE.md). Unconfirmed instance: shrink-test saw requests at 18:20:59 and 18:24:08 CST open 6ab855c9 (default's 17:31 publication) through that path although the cluster record named 6ab86150; the note attributes them to pid 50733, which started only at 18:26:24 CST, so they ran on the JVM before it. Key the loaded identity by the store whose program the JVM loaded, and never let an adoption on another store move it."
             :must-read #{seon.cluster/development-source-refresh! seon.sci.eval/loaded-identity seon.test/arm-first-loads!}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/perf-boot-opus-2026-09-26.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "mcp-reads-the-jvm-wide-instance-roster"
             :kind :function
             :intent "mcp-instance reads seon.operator.runtime/running-instances directly with no way to pass an instance, so mcp-test fixtures swap! the JVM-wide roster 16 times (JVM-global test state) and one test builds its context with env/carry-state {} and with-redefs over config/effective. Pass the instance through the mcp-* functions (mcp-valf, mcp-get-value, mcp-effective, runtime observation) and convert the fixtures to injected instances."
             :must-read #{seon.cluster/mcp-get-value}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/red-triage-3-2026-09-27.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "mcp-reply-without-a-database-prints-unbounded"
             :kind :function
             :intent "In JVM mode for a cluster with no connection (before the store layer is up, or a cluster name this JVM does not host), mcp-project has no database for render.value/prepare, whose unit requires :seon.db/db; the refusal is attached and the value falls back to plain printing with the MCP profile's budget unapplied. AGENTS: nothing prints unbounded. The fallback prints through the floor's bounded path (bounded-text), never plain Clojure printing of the whole value (fix-c, 4c2ac5774)."
             :must-read #{seon.cluster/mcp-project seon.render.value/prepare}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/red-triage-3-2026-09-27.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:id "e4f90fb37e0c"
             :name "incremental-publication-test-redefines-process-wide-vars"
             :kind :function
             :intent "seon.incremental-publication-test/non-program-inputs-have-their-own-publication-owner points publication at a fixture checkout with with-redefs-fn over clojure.java.io/resource and seon.cluster/publication-roots. Both are Var roots, so every thread of the shared JVM (default's agents, other test members) reads the fixture's schemas and roots while it runs. Give refresh-source! a source seam (publication roots and the schema resource directory passed as values) so the test hands its checkout, or declare the test isolated until then."
             :must-read #{seon.cluster/refresh-source! seon.cluster/publication-roots}
             :evidence #{"test/seon/incremental_publication_test.clj"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "schema-adoption-refuses-instead-of-dropping-an-edn-encoded-value"
             :kind :function
             :intent "invalid-value-retraction decodes each stored value with seon.schema.datahike/decode-attribute-value-in, which for an EDN-encoded attribute validates the decoded value against the attribute's NEW form and throws ::schema-invalid (datahike.clj:328-331). So a narrowed EDN-encoded attribute makes the whole adoption throw instead of retracting only the refused values, and an EDN-encoded cardinality-many attribute would validate one member against its whole [:vector ...] form. No installed many attribute is EDN-encoded today (117 probed on default, 2026-09-27), so the many case is latent. Decode without the slot validation here (the retraction validates), or share the writer's attribute plan (db.clj write-attribute-plan)."
             :must-read #{seon.cluster/invalid-value-retraction seon.schema.datahike/decode-attribute-value-in}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/register-anywhere-diagnosis-2026-09-27.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:id "47491ad902b3"
             :name "runtime-status-throws-on-a-boot-window-read"
